        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>A VLAN (Virtual Local Area Network) logically separates a single physical network into multiple isolated virtual networks.</p><h3>Why Use VLANs?</h3><p>Security and performance. For example, you can put Guest Wi-Fi on VLAN 10 and Corporate devices on VLAN 20. Even though they share the same physical switches, they cannot communicate unless routed through a firewall.</p>
        </div>
        
